===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|quadrant}}, from {{der|en|fro|cadran}}, {{m|fro|quadrant}} and its etymon {{der|en|la|quadrāns}}, {{m|la||-antis|fourth part of something, quarter}}.<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=quā̆drant|pos=''n.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED35388}}</ref> {{doublet|en|quadrans}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# One of the four [[section]]s made by dividing an area with two perpendicular lines.
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2007|actor={{w|Vernon Chatman|Vernon Chatman}}|role=Xavier|title={{w|Xavier: Renegade Angel|Xavier: Renegade Angel}}|season=1|number=4|text=Kids, I swear, I'm gonna love all of you, and equally. I'll be dividing my love into seven equal sections, or "Love '''Quadrants'''". Each '''quadrant''' will be worth 15 "Love Units" represented by these small brass marbles. You may use these marbles as currency amongst yourselves. Collect 35 "Love Units", you can trade those in for a beach towel with my face on it.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} One of the four regions of the [[Cartesian plane]] bounded by the [[x-axis]] and [[y-axis]].
# {{senseid|en|geometry quarter circle}}{{lb|en|geometry}} One [[fourth]] of a [[circle]] or [[disc]]; a sector with an [[angle]] of 90&deg;.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[measuring]] [[device]] with a graduated arc of 90&deg; used in locating an altitude.
# {{lb|en|college basketball}} One of the four categories of team wins and losses, as categorized by strength of schedule.

